    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 the single test class (`AcceptanceTest`) passes, and the audit log confirms a new owner lands at `membershipLevel=3`.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe spec's substantive requirement is that **level 4 is gated behind tenure > 365 days**, and a brand-new owner (zero tenure) never exceeds level 3.\n\n**`model/MembershipLevel.java`** \u2014 added the tenure-gated top level while keeping the existing factor logic intact:\n- The email + no-namesakes bonuses still cap at `MAX = 3` (the \"pre-tenure factors\").\n- A new `TENURE_MAX = 4` level is reached by a single extra bump, granted only when tenure exceeds `TENURE_DAYS = 365` days (registration date to `asOf`).\n- Followed the existing `AgeBand.of(owner, asOf)` pattern: a testable `of(Owner, LocalDate)` overload plus a convenience `of(Owner)` that uses `LocalDate.now()` (consistent with how the rest of the codebase reads the current date). Tenure math lives in a small private `hasTenure` helper, so no method becomes a catch-all.\n\n**`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 updated the javadoc from \"1 to 3\" to \"1 to 4\" to match.\n\nFor the tested scenario (new owner, email present, `namesakeCount = 0`): `1 + 1 + 1 = 3`, capped at `MAX`; tenure is 0 days so no bump \u2192 **level 3**, exactly as required. Level 4 only appears once such an owner has been registered for more than a year.\n\nNote: I did **not** add a `householdMemberCount` factor. The current level formula never used it, the \"3-member household\" in the test appears only as descriptive context (\"a well-qualified new owner still caps at 3\"), and the spec gives no household threshold \u2014 so inventing one would be speculative untested logic rather than a real requirement. If a household factor *is* intended, let me know the threshold and I'll fold it into `MembershipLevel` as another pre-tenure bonus.",
